From: =?UTF-8?q?=E9=9B=AA=E8=8E=B9=E3=81=A1=E3=82=83=E3=82=93?=
 <151988757+SnowGlow-aww@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 04:18:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] fix(handler,search): apply the masterdata world bloom
 finale rules to JP #218

JP #218 is a real World Link finale (worldBlooms chapterType "finale")
but only the ids 180 and 3_200_000 were treated as finales, so it was
searched as an ordinary WL3 chapter.

- Detect finales from worldBlooms in addition to the two fixed ids and
  route every handler/search finale check through EventContext::is_finale.
- eventSkillScoreUpLimits.scoreUpRateLimit is the skill effect cap itself
  (140 = 140%, same unit as the 180 fallback); stop subtracting 100.
- Read the optional eventShuffleUnitBonuses table and add the bonus for
  the number of distinct units in the main deck (Virtual Singers count
  only as VIRTUAL SINGER). A missing or empty table adds nothing. Search
  bounds add the exact bonus once the unit set is fixed and otherwise the
  largest rate still reachable, so they stay admissible.
- The member-count limit fallback stays 4 only for 180 and 3_200_000;
  masterdata finales without a row (JP #218) get 5.
